# Google Cloud multi-account (binding)

## Purpose

Developers may sign into **multiple Google accounts** on one machine. Documentation
Management missions and skills must **not** clobber the machine-wide gcloud active
account or interfere with dispatches on **other hosting repos**.

Normative **`gcloud` install** registry: **`rules/10_required-tools.mdc`**. Drive
setup owner: **`missions/required-tools-installation/skills/configure-gcloud-drive/SKILL.md`**.

## Additive authentication (binding)

| Rule | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| User auth | **`mission_control_start_interactive_terminal`** preset **`gcloud`** in **lane waiting mode**; **configure-gcloud-drive** §1.0 asks **use existing** vs **add another** when accounts exist; post-login gate per §1b.3 — **forbidden:** agent **Shell** interactive login; **forbidden:** background invocation |
| Agent shells | **Forbidden:** interactive **`gcloud auth login`** — use interactive-terminal MCP preset **`gcloud`** per **configure-gcloud-drive** §1b |
| Revoke | **Forbidden:** **`gcloud auth revoke`** (any account) in agent shells without explicit user structured-choice consent |

## Account binding (binding)

The Google account for **this hosting repo** is bound during **configure-gcloud-drive**
and recorded in terminal skill outputs:

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **`gcloudAccountEmail`** | User Google account email used for this hosting repo's GCP/Drive setup |
| **`gcloudConfigurationName`** | Named gcloud configuration id (see below) — documentation only; **never activate** in agent shells |

Other missions **must** read **`gcloudAccountEmail`** from configure handover or prior
spawn outputs — **forbidden:** inferring account from **`gcloud auth list --filter=status:ACTIVE`**
or the global active account alone.

## Every agent-shell `gcloud` call (binding — all lanes)

Before any **`gcloud`** command in an **agent** shell (including **configure-gcloud-drive**):

```bash
export CLOUDSDK_CORE_DISABLE_PROMPTS=1
export GCLOUD_ACCOUNT="<gcloudAccountEmail>"   # after account is bound for this pass
```

**Required on every `gcloud` invocation:**

- **`--account="${GCLOUD_ACCOUNT}"`** (or equivalent explicit email flag)
- **`--project="<projectId>"`** when the command is project-scoped — prefer the flag
  over mutating default project state

Optional belt-and-suspenders: **`export CLOUDSDK_AUTH_ACCOUNT="${GCLOUD_ACCOUNT}"`**
— **does not** replace **`--account`** on commands.

**Forbidden in all agent shells (including configure-gcloud-drive):**

| Pattern | Why |
|---------|-----|
| **`gcloud config set account`** | Mutates global or named-config account binding — breaks other hosting repos |
| **`gcloud config configurations activate`** | Switches machine-wide active configuration |
| **`gcloud config set project`** without **`--configuration=`** | Mutates global default project |
| Relying on **`status:ACTIVE`** from **`gcloud auth list`** as authority | Wrong account when multiple repos/users share one machine |

Dry-runs in **`10_required-tools.mdc`** (**`gcloud version`**, **`gcloud help`**) are
**CLI-only** and do not require **`--account`**.

## Named configuration (configure-gcloud-drive only)

**Purpose:** Persist **project default** per hosting repo without activating a config
or changing the global active account.

| Step | Command (example) |
|------|-------------------|
| Derive name | **`sedea-<hosting-basename>`** where **`<hosting-basename>`** is **`HOSTING_ROOT`** directory basename |
| Create (idempotent) | **`gcloud config configurations create "<name>" --no-activate`** |
| Set project on named config | **`gcloud config set project "<projectId>" --configuration="<name>"`** |

**Forbidden:** **`gcloud config set account`** on any configuration; **`gcloud config configurations activate`**.

Record **`gcloudConfigurationName`** in configure terminal outputs.

## Non-configure missions

Missions that do not run **configure-gcloud-drive** typically use **rclone** with
service-account JSON flags (**`10_required-tools.mdc`** § Drive auth invoke). When they
**do** invoke **`gcloud`**, apply **Every agent-shell `gcloud` call** above using the
bound **`gcloudAccountEmail`**.

